# =============================================================================
# Kaata env reference — local development overview.
# =============================================================================
# This file is a high-level pointer. Each app owns its own env file:
#
#   apps/backend/.env.example  → copy to apps/backend/.env
#   apps/web/.env.example      → copy to apps/web/.env.local
#   apps/mobile/.env.example   → copy to apps/mobile/.env.local
#
# `bun dev` runs all three with their respective env loaders (godotenv for
# Go, Vite for web, Expo for mobile). There is no root .env loader — this
# file exists only as a map.
#
# For production deployment values (Dokploy services, EAS Build), see
# `.env.production` at the repo root and the matching `.env.production`
# files inside each app folder.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev quick-start
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Bring up a local Postgres 18 on :5432 (or run
#    `psql -f apps/backend/scripts/setup-dev-db.sql` against an existing one).
# 2. Copy each app's .env.example to its real env file (see paths above).
# 3. Run `bun dev` from the repo root.
#
# Defaults assume:
#   - Backend at  http://localhost:8080
#   - Web at      http://localhost:3000
#   - Mobile via  Expo Go (LAN IP) or simulator (localhost / 10.0.2.2)


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Variables at a glance (full docs in each app's .env.example)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend (apps/backend/.env):
#   POSTGRES_URL, BACKEND_PORT, APK_DOWNLOAD_URL, MIGRATE_TO_BACKEND_URL,
#   GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID (Google sign-in audience),
#   APPLE_CLIENT_ID (Apple sign-in audience; defaults to af.kaata.app),
#   JWT_SECRET (session JWTs; legacy alias SESSION_JWT_SECRET),
#   ADMIN_API_KEY (+ OPERATOR_* filters) for the /admin dashboard,
#   WEB_BASE_URL / SHARE_LINK_BASE_URL / PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL (shared links),
#   MESH_SIGNING_* (parked mesh), BACKEND_DEVICE_ID + KAATA_ENV (prod checks)
#
# Web (apps/web/.env.local):
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL, VITE_WHATSAPP_CONTACT_URL,
#   VITE_APK_VERSION, VITE_APK_DOWNLOAD_URL
#
# Mobile (apps/mobile/.env.local):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL, EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID,
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLO_STORE_MODE
#   (production builds get EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL + EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLO_STORE_MODE
#   from apps/mobile/eas.json; EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID is NOT set
#   there — builds fall back to the default in apps/mobile/constants/env.ts.
#   Sign in with Apple needs no env var — audience = iOS bundle id in
#   app.json; the backend's APPLE_CLIENT_ID must match it.)
